    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1064-a11">

                <pb facs="1156" n="1060" sameAs="frus:frus1898/pg1060"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 11 in No. 267.]</seg><lb/><dateline
                        rendition="#center">[Copy of telegram in reply <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1898-02-17">February 17, 1898</date>.]</dateline></opener>
                <p rendition="#flush">The Right Hon. The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lord
                    Mayor</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic">Mansion House, E. C.:</hi></p>
                <p>In the absence of the ambassador in Egypt, I beg to acknowledge the receipt of,
                    and to thank your lordship most sincerely for, your telegram of sympathy in
                    respect to the disaster to the <hi rendition="#italic">Maine</hi>, which I at
                    once cabled to my Government. My countrymen will appreciate highly the sympathy
                    of the citizens of London and of the chief magistrate.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Henry White</hi>, <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Chargé d’Affaires.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
